From 30f9c1a213521aab2e8d9a62d50544163fab7329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:59:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add organization and collaborator visibility

Repos are now fetched with affiliation=owner,organization_member,collaborator so
personal, organization, and collaborator repos all appear on the dashboard.

Projects page groups repos into three sections:
- "Your projects" (owned by the logged-in user) with the New project button
- One section per GitHub organization the user belongs to, labelled with an "org" badge
- "Collaborations" for repos owned by other individual users, showing the owner name

Routes updated from /p/:repo to /p/:owner/:repo so any repo can be opened
regardless of who owns it. Files.jsx and History.jsx now read owner from the
URL param instead of assuming auth.user.login, so saves and history work
correctly for org and collab repos.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FWksNavChAtxifMa2DCfS4
